<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sun Quan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">182–252</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Emperor Da of Wu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sun Quan was the founder of the state of Eastern Wu in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms period</a>. Allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bei">Liu Bei</a>, he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-cao">Cao Cao</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-red-cliffs">Battle of Red Cliffs</a> in 208, then turned on Shu Han, taking Jing province in 219 and defeating Liu Bei at Xiaoting in 222. He proclaimed himself emperor in 229 with his capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiankang">Jianye</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sun-quan.jpg" alt="Sun Quan" width="320" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yan Liben · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sun_Quan_Tang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
